{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1364278-aberrant-transformers","id":1364278,"title":"Aberrant: Transformers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-30T20:57:48-08:00","id":1364278,"title":"Aberrant: Transformers","content":"Don't have the kickstarter rules so just playing around with this idea based on a vague notion of how they work.<br /> <br /> A transformation power that turns the user into a starship. For extra fun rule that the warp and teleport powers have their base and extended distances increased by 10^scale. It's simply that nobody realized you could do it during the nova age. Add in some form of quantum construct so that the character has an avatar on the ship and work it so that the character can control drones when the party isn't aboard.<br /> <br /> Or um, just use transformation into various vehicles and giant fighting robots if starships are not your style. Assuming that quantum construct makes it into the new edition, you can create construct drivers or crew, which might have some advantages in causing enemies to attack the construct and not the vehicle/character.<br /> <br /> Quantum construct, mega intelligence, the 1e molecular manipulation power that allows for transformation into complex objects and an aberrant version of the code power from trinity. Turn everyday objects into transforming robots. Actually, you can model with just with 1e quantum construct but again, it's probably getting nerfed Might also setup some rapid gadgetering fun (if that's going to be allowed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"